WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.150
If you've ever wondered how superheroes manage
to do all that heroic stuff while wearing

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.350
those wildly impractical costumes, you're
not alone.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.130
In fact, some of the actors playing these
heroes on the big screen had major issues

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.290
with their outfits.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.769
Here's a look at some actors who despised
their superhero costumes.

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.780
Jennifer Lawrence

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.280
That blue body paint that Jennifer Lawrence
wears in the X-Men films may look cool, but

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.580
J-Law herself isn't a huge fan considering
it took a whopping seven hours to apply when

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.720
she filmed X-Men: First Class — not to mention
all those iffy chemicals.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.450
She told Entertainment Weekly that she worries
about the fumes and toxins now that she's

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.450
older.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.640
"I’m almost 25 and I’m like, ‘I can’t
even pronounce this and that’s going in

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.640
my nose?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.640
I’m breathing that?’”

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.250
Luckily, the makeup process was cut down to
approximately three hours for Days of Future

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.130
Past and Apocalypse, thanks in part to a new
body suit they created.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.329
That's evolution in action!

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:53.329
Ron Perlman

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:56.970
J-Law isn't the only hero who's sick of the
makeup chair.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.420
Ron Perlman had to endure marathon sessions
for his role as Hellboy, as it took between

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.630
four and seven hours for him to get ready
every time thanks to the use of old school

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.729
prosthetics rather than CGI.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:12.679
In fact, director Guillermo del Toro told
Den of Geek that Perlman's hatred of the costume

00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:16.039
is one major reason there hasn't been a third
Hellboy film.

00:01:16.039 --> 00:01:19.999
"He really grew tired of the makeup in the
second film and he was really rubbed the wrong

00:01:19.999 --> 00:01:21.789
way by those seven-hour sessions."

00:01:21.789 --> 00:01:24.770
Sounds like…hell...boy.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.209
Ryan Reynolds

00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:31.179
Unlike many superhero movie stars, Ryan Reynolds
didn't have to go through an arduous process

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:34.729
to get in costume for Green Lantern, thanks
to the fact that his suit was mostly done

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:35.729
with CGI.

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:37.899
So why does Reynolds hate the costume?

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:40.130
Because it looks crappy, and he loathes the
movie.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.810
“I would, I would give it a scant…”

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.580
“...four, maybe.”

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.380
“You would give it a four?”

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.280
“Yeah a three or a four.”

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.039
“You would give it a three or four?”

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:49.760
“Yeah it didn’t work.”

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:50.760
“It didn’t work?”

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:51.260
“Yeah...one!

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.060
It’s a one!”

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.580
How much did he dislike his costume in the
Green Lantern?

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.200
He even made fun of it on screen in his hit
superhero parody Deadpool.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.749
“And please don’t make the supersuit green.

00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:01.749
Or animated!”

00:02:01.749 --> 00:02:03.579
Paul Bettany

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:07.819
Back when he was providing the voice of Tony
Stark's JARVIS computer-guy in the Iron Man

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:12.351
films, Paul Bettany said he felt like "a pirate"
because the voiceover work was so easy it

00:02:12.351 --> 00:02:13.470
was like stealing money.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.240
Well, he quickly learned that he was going
to have to earn his money as The Vision, because

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.650
now that he's on screen, he has to endure
his own uncomfortable costume, which he told

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.439
USA Today takes three and a half hours to
put on.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:27.969
"By the fourth and fifth day of the week,
you are really having to meditate on the line

00:02:27.969 --> 00:02:31.150
of actors, thousands of them, who would love
to be in your position.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.340
You have to concentrate on how lucky you are."

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.340
Christian Bale

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:39.980
With three Batman movies under his utility
belt, Christian Bale is something of an expert

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.060
on the importance of a comfortable costume.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.810
After enduring a terribly constricting and
painful suit for Batman Begins, Bale requested

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.040
a new suit for The Dark Knight, resulting
in more fluid action scenes and a more relaxed

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.310
filming experience.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.859
But his biggest piece of advice for future
Batmen, like Ben Affleck?

00:02:55.859 --> 00:02:58.060
Make sure your batsuit has a zipper on it.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.180
“Oh, the only thing I said to him is ‘Look,
just make sure he can take a piss without

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:06.200
anyone having to help him, because it’s
a little bit humiliating,’ as I went through

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.480
when you have to have somebody you know, kinda...help
you out.”

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.079
Val Kilmer

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:16.489
If only Christian Bale had been around to
share that bit of potty advice to Val Kilmer.

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:22.030
Turns out Kilmer, who played the Caped Crusader
in 1995's Batman Forever, also had major issues

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:26.469
with his costume, including an unfortunate
inability to use the restroom alone.

00:03:26.469 --> 00:03:30.260
He likened wearing his suit, which took an
hour to put on, to living in an old folk's

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.260
home.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.069
"I realized one day what wearing that suit
was like.

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:34.579
It was, ‘Oh!

00:03:34.579 --> 00:03:36.510
This is what being old feels like.’

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.040
No one really listens to you any more.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.709
You can’t really talk or hear.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:44.730
You’re always falling over and someone has
to help you go to the bathroom and get dressed."

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.849
Anne Hathaway

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:48.829
Some superhero costumes are uncomfortable.

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:52.840
And then there's the signature skintight suit
and heels of Catwoman, which was even more

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.069
uncomfortable mentally than physically for
Dark Knight Rises star Anne Hathaway, as she

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.799
explained in an interview with Allure.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:01.109
"[The costume] was a psychological terrorist.

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:06.400
The suit, thoughts of my suit, changing my
life so I would fit into that suit…It dominated

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.400
my year.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.519
I went to the gym for ten months and didn't
come out."

00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:12.099
Robert Downey, Jr.

00:04:12.099 --> 00:04:16.100
As you've probably learned by now, it's tough
being a superhero, something Robert Downey,

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.380
Jr. learned the hard way when he stepped into
the role of Iron Man.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.960
"I'd been training all these years and thought
I was pretty tough, but the first time I put

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.920
on the Mark 1 suit, I almost had a personality
meltdown.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.040
I'm not claustrophobic, but after moving around
in it for a couple of hours, your spirit is

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.340
kind of broken and you're like, 'Okay, time
to bring in the stunt team.'"

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.830
Fortunately, these days most of the time Marvel
Studios is able to render the suit with CGI

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.950
rather than grape jelly.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:42.490
“Whoo!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.300
Hoooaaahhh!”

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.040
Thanks for watching!

